namespace OpenTPW.UI.Original;

/// <summary>
/// Register of every UI value or rule that is not taken from original data or hard evidence
/// (docs/UI.md "Approximation register"). Each site carries a matching
/// <c>// [APPROX:UI-NNN]</c> comment; <see cref="LogOnce"/> reports them at startup.
/// </summary>
public static class UiApproximations
{
	public static readonly IReadOnlyList<(string Id, string Assumption, string EvidenceNeeded)> All = new[]
	{
		("UI-003", "the state selection of the original UI model draw beyond the stored selected-mesh endpoints is not traced; the instance traverser 0x57a530 composes each node's world matrix from its local matrix and its ancestors' (the root starts as its local matrix times the caller's, the identity set at 0x57a55b being overwritten), OpenTPW does the same, no ui.wad child carries a rotation or scale (only translations, which cancel in the selected-mesh fit), and the window angle (+0xe2) is ported as DrawFrame's turn (0x476c50)", "the UI control draw's selection of a state frame"),
		("UI-004", "UI model triangles drawn back to front by Z, grouped per texture; the original draws a UI model as nodes of the scene instance list: the walker 0x576910 (it sets global 0x8bb624 to 0x1000000 while it walks, which 0x581cd0 reads at 0x581cf6, 0x581cff and 0x581d15) appends their parts through the traverser 0x57a530 and 0x581cd0, and the frame batcher 0x581db0 gives every part its state word from its texture's alpha type (0x581790 -> 0x590c40, so a cut-out interface texture is tested at 0xf0/255 like a world texture), draws the states of bits 0x1000 and 0x2000 at once in file order with depth test and depth write on (decoder 0x567620 bits 0x8000 and 0x800 absent) and defers the others, far to near by the part's average depth (0x5829e0) with their triangles sorted by depth sum (0x565490); a part whose material word has bit 0x2 (state bit 0x800000, no shipped material) is keyed by its index span at 0x58109e instead; the display object's UI depth range is [0, 0.1) in front of [0.1, 0.2) and [0.2, 1) (defaults 0x582db4-0x582dc1), but how a UI vertex's depth reaches it (the transform at 0x87b1d8 +0xc) and whether the UI pass shares or clears the scene's depth buffer are not read, so the depth-tested file order is not ported", "the depth value the UI vertex transform (0x87b1d8 +0xc, called at 0x581092) gives a UI vertex, and whether the depth buffer is cleared between the scene and the UI nodes"),
		("UI-006", "text colours: window titles and the lobby island name yellow, the object windows' labels and values white, the pause menu's lines cyan (white while focused), green values elsewhere, grey disabled, the texture-switch progress bar track and backdrop colours (the video's 720p chroma is good to about +-15 per channel); the original gives each text control an RGBA colour (0x65c5d5 → renderer +0x48, kept as ARGB at +0x78, 0x48fd07; the sprite draw 0x58a010 takes it as the diffuse colour of the control's quads, 0x58a019) and renders its glyphs white (0x48fa96) unless the control keeps the font's own colours (+0xdd); the values traced are the options labels' (0,0,0,255) (0x4a441e), the buy list rows' (255,255,255,255) (0x4ad340), the pause menu lines' (0,175,190,255) (0x48b2b9) and the shared title colour (234,239,102,255) (0x492d20, fifteen window builders), with the lobby island name's second line (252,232,7,255) (0x4b8604) and a list row control that turns (140,0,60) on message 0x403 with a negative argument (0x4a0710); the other 0x65c5d5 calls (134 sites in all; by an instruction scan: about 36 with white (255,255,255,255), 31 with black (0,0,0,255) such as the runs 0x49ada6-0x49b385 and 0x4a53a2-0x4a5d26, 7 with red (255,0,0,255) at 0x49ff69, 0x4a002f, 0x4a6273 and 0x4b2e93-0x4b31f7, 5 with (224,86,86,255) at 0x4aa82d-0x4aac70, and about 45 that pass the colour from registers or tables) are not yet assigned to screens", "which screen each remaining 0x65c5d5 call colours (values, disabled states, costs) and the backdrop colours"),
		("UI-008", "text buttons without a UI model on purple_button art (ui.wad ships purple_button.wct, but no UI model of ui.wad names it and tp.exe holds no 'purple' string: the PC's labelled buttons are model-backed, b_login (button_text1, button_text2), b_dellog (b_pinkbutt, b_pinkbuttd), b_loantog (b_text, paybck, paybckd), and b_okay and b_exit through the dialog builder 0x47f020), so which art, if any, a PC screen gives a model-less text button is unread; each half is one end cap, drawn with its mirror image; upper half normal, lower half focused/pressed", "which PC screens draw a text button without a model and with which art (the name resolver 0x659bc9 and the UI model loader 0x488D20's state-to-texture mapping), or a capture of the original front-end buttons"),
		("UI-018", "the lobby draws the engine sky's cloud layer (sky.tga, coloured by the eased island colour) over the fog-coloured clear, without fog (the lobby's range 50 to 300 is set but the scene clears the fog enable, 0x5d8bf9; RenderFog, UI-107); while the globe is up the lobby's flyers and island clips keep stepping (the original's per-frame lobby update 0x5d5c50 has no globe branch and the main state stays 2, 0x54e6c7) but the island effects (lightning, thunder, rain, the nearest-island sky target) do not, where the islands component 0x5e0470 probably runs before the globe component sets the sky target and no rain each frame; whether the lobby scene is drawn then is not traced; the enter sequence is built (the camera turns to the island angle + π, the gate plays M1, the camera zooms under the black fade and the park starts below radius 8, 0x5e0490 states 1 and 2; an early leave's gate M2 close, 0x5e1350, is not reachable from the front end here); the key-unlock sequence is not traced", "the sky flags that enable the engine sky's draw (0x576a00), the registration order of the lobby's subsystems while the globe is up and whether the scene is drawn then, the key-award animation's code"),
		("UI-024", "the object windows (tables 0x755150, 0x755908, 0x755e80) draw their controls at the table rectangles and, for a shop or sideshow, the customer satisfaction gauge from the object's visit history (0x4e1e30), but the preview is OpenTPW's orthographic icon ([EXT:preview-icon-cpu-projection]); the local happiness gauge is 0x4cd880's mean over the 3 × 3 cells around the object's cell (every guest in the cell lists, the happiness float cut to a byte, the unsigned clamp of the high edge at 0x7f), as ported; the original takes the cell from the thing's own byte pair (+5, +7), which OpenTPW reads as the placement anchor, and its low edge wraps (x - 1 below 0 reads the last cell of the previous row, which is ported; y - 1 below 0 reads past the cell table, which no object reaches, since only owned land holds objects and the west and north fence lines are never owned); the build window fits the preview size to translated names and prices", "the thing cell byte pair (+5, +7) an object keeps and whether it is the placement anchor"),
		("UI-025", "the message tube admits ten occupied slots and refuses all new rows when full without eviction, sound or help (the tube's add routine 0x48EB20, the cap word 0x750610 = 10), and is saved with the park as an optional validated part of the resume save (the original's saver 0x48EE50, loader 0x48EF70); challenge progress refreshes tagged rows at capacity, while new progress/terminal rows refuse full occupancy; terminal instances survive reading/closing, expire unread after 30 unscaled seconds, and retain hidden slots for 500 ms after expiry/deletion; cross-tag replacement is synchronous; an offer is a tube row with the original's 90 s expiry and 5 s earlier warning timers, stays when read and, when deleted, expired or answered, is hidden and removed 500 ms later with the decline run first (0x48db94, 0x48e269; an answered offer's decline does nothing), and is never opened by itself (0x48edeb is dead: the record builder 0x509bf0 clears the byte it tests); generic messages still leave on open where the original keeps every tag until it is deleted, answered or expired; the tube art remains an extension", "the full timer queue/focus/modal integration, the other action-bearing sources and the tube's keep-until-deleted rule for generic messages (the tag lifetimes of every message tag); the original's own save record (OpenTPW writes its own JSON part and does not import an original save's tag block); visual validation and UI particles (PTCL-908)"),
		("UI-026", "build icons: the preview model (P<name>.MD2, else the main model) is drawn depth tested in its own image ([EXT:preview-icon-cpu-projection]) with the original's placement, camera and face test: the fit and footprint terms of 0x4689f0, the matrix 0x468e50 rebuilds each frame (the yaw and the -π/4 tilt through the sine table, the offsets, x scaled by 0.75 and depth by 0.1), the instance's own view diag(1, -1, 1, 1) (0x45bd30, 0x57a260, used for model flag 0x200 by 0x57a750), the viewport mapping with depth × 0.1 (0x579690 mode 2), the clockwise-only face test (0x581320) and LESSEQUAL depth (0x567620, 0x57360f), its turn of 0.0004 rad a millisecond running on across selections (0x46908a, 0x468e2f), and animation 5 started on each new preview (0x4732a0: <model>m1, else <model>m, looping); but the original lights the preview's vertices in its 3D object pipeline (0x57aa10) and OpenTPW draws them unlit; the selected item's footprint grid (8×8 cells coloured by cell type in control 0x1eb, 0x4ab1b0, record 0x754d50) is built (BuyFootprint), with the 1-pixel edges of its cell rectangles not traced; the object windows' previews keep a 30° tilt and 0.8 rad/s; sign faces use the object's rendered sign textures (ObjectSigns)", "the light set the 3D pipeline gives an instance drawn with its own view (0x57aa10 with the instance's second matrix slot +0x50, which 0x45bd30 does not write) and the pixel edges of the footprint cells"),
		("UI-031", "exactly Ctrl at the placing click keeps the build tool armed (0x5253b8; the Move tool's 0x5259e2), a ride with an entrance takes the queue tool after its placement whatever the modifier (0x52f580(3, 0)), and the queue tool's last click ends the tool whatever the modifier (0x5275b1..0x5275f2: 0x52f200(0, 0) sets mode 0 and replaces the build tool object, its mode 4 or 0x3b with its type, by the default tool), the tool's angle returning to 0 when it is left (0x52f3b6); the coaster tool ends the build tool at the placement whatever the modifier; the kart and water line tools (0xB, 0x10) take the queue tool when their circuit closes only while the placement's queue start 0x8186c0 is pending (0x526f95, 0x527004), from the cell the last placement stored (0x7639b8/0x7639bc), and the handover takes it (0x527056), as build and Move clicks on an accepted ghost (a click on a refused ghost returns at the latch first, 0x524a63), the Move pick-up and path or queue commits drop it (0x524b53, 0x5253f3, 0x525e5a, 0x527483), a path start cell ending the queue tool at once (0x52712f), and with no queue start exactly Ctrl keeps the line tool without a start (0x527146) and any other word ends it (0x527156); the Ctrl word 0xC at 0x5259e2/0x5259f4 is Ctrl alone (the modifier builder 0x46b420: Shift 3, Ctrl 0xC, Alt 0x30) and a placement that 0x52fab0 reports as entrance-bearing (the sub-record flag +0x40) takes the tail 0x5259ae: the queue re-evaluation 0x4de1f0, the words 0x763ac0 and 0x763ac4 back to 0x80, then the map cell record +0x29c (the cell's type word, +8 of the 0x44-byte record at +0x294) of the queue's start cell that 0x52a050 gave decides at 0x5259cf: type 1 (a path cell) ends the tool through 0x52f200(0, 0) whatever the modifier, which returns the angle to 0 as well (0x52f3b6); for any other start cell the mode stays the queue tool 3 that 0x52f580 set before, exactly Ctrl keeps the angle through it (0x525a06) and any other word runs 0x52f1b0(0, 0), which resets it (OpenTPW keeps the angle through the queue tool whatever the modifier and resets it when the queue tool ends); the coaster sub-mode (0x52faf0 = 3) takes the same tail and skips only the kart and water station line, so the tail itself enters the queue tool for a coaster as well, and the coaster's track tool (mode 0x15, 0x4474d0) is not entered anywhere in 0x524960; its click hands over to the queue tool when the pass 0x81 returns 0 (0x526525) only while a queue start is pending (0x52656e, taken at 0x526680), and otherwise ends the tool (0x5266bc), where OpenTPW's coaster tool enters the queue tool of a ride with one when the coaster is completed, pending start or not; which OpenTPW placements end at 0x5259cf is not mapped; Level.PlaceObject owns purchase/guest linkage and its removal handler owns scrap credits", "the original's coaster placement enters the queue tool, not its track tool: mode 0x15 with the coaster sub-mode 3 (0x497d20) is entered only by the ride window's track button (0x4af200 → 0x4af275 → 0x4988c0), by a click on the coaster in the park (class 6, 0x487e56 → 0x487eeb → 0x4988c0, which enters it while 0x441910 says the track is not complete) and by the coaster window's button 0x1f (0x498333), so OpenTPW's entry at the placement is the difference still to port; the pass 0x81 returns 0 for a line whose last cell met an existing path or queue cell (0x5340a5 with the flag 0x820abc set at 0x5345ad), which takes 0x526568, and any other result falls to 0x526527; which of OpenTPW's placements have a path cell as the queue's start"),
		("UI-042", "the camera button's slide-out panel (table 0x751720) slides in and out as the arm drawer 0x4a14f0 does (ten 20 ms steps, cat_ui 0x1C and 0xC2, help 0x131): the drawer places the panel at the arm's left less the panel's own width and a horizontal gap of 50 (0x4a1631, the width read by 0x659e3e), centred vertically on the arm (the arm's top plus half the arm's height less half the panel's, 0x4a163b-0x4a1647) and then moves it right by a tenth of (the HUD window's right edge - the arm's left + the panel's width + 100) each step (0x4a16e5, the step 0x4a1704, the tick 0x4a19e7), the step being the integer quotient by the tick count 10 and the ten ticks adding it, so the panel ends at its start plus 10 times that step (the camera panel at left 482, top 1206; the message panel through the same drawer at left 486, top 1112) with the arm's art (bar, pane and handle) growing out from under the HUD; the camcorder button arms the C-key walk ([EXT:camcorder-first-person]) where the original's button 99 enters the camcorder at once (0x498ad0 → 0x481a10), and the walk's movement and look controls are not traced (the original's eye is terrain + 5 units, 0x42b1c0); the postcard window (table 0x7540d8) keeps its photo frame empty and its preview button disabled (the 640×240 camcorder photo 0x4a9280 and the preview redraw 0x4a84c0 are not ported); its address book (table 0x7542b8, 0x4a8140) and its sending through OpenTPW's own server are not part of this ID ([EXT:online-postcard-address-book], user-approved 2026-10-30); the original has no view-cycle button, so OpenTPW has none (0x751720 holds only the two buttons; no window control changes the zoom or yaw, and the locate jumps 0x42aab0 pass null zoom and yaw)", "the walk's key bindings (action table 0x787c14) and the time unit of its turn step; the photo and its preview"),
		("UI-060", "finance retains the eight series colours/order, selection masks, default bank balance, zero-inclusive scale, flat baseline, fractional series coordinates and hollow 3 x 3 pixel marks below 144 samples. Finance and park information share the opaque black backdrop, dark-green grid (0,100,0), green axes/step labels (0,200,0), plot (4,4,width-20,height-20), ten horizontal divisions and twelve labeled vertical spans for 12/36/144 samples (0x4806a0, 0x47fb50, 0x47fcd0); grid coordinates accumulate stored floats and truncate, primitive lengths are pixel counts (the pixel size itself, two canvas units and at least one framebuffer pixel, is the host adapter [EXT:graph-pixel-adapter], user-approved 2026-10-30, not part of this ID), and the negative-minimum zero axis omits the bottom branch's extra pixel (0x47fc50). Empty histories and selections keep the backdrop. Signed 128-bit axis arithmetic for long financial values, background-only tiny/unsupported host controls and nonfinite-frame rejection are host safety adaptations", "the placement of fewer months than the period (the samples themselves are the ring's months, 1:1, 0x480460) and OpenTPW's stretching of the available months; font, palette, raster and composited-output fidelity; a rendered composition of the graphs"),
		("UI-082", "the hire figure uses the traced inner rectangle, integer feet (626,362) and nominal 2.4 canvas units per reference pixel; it is the script's own sprite (0x74F758: flags 0x51000 and heading 5 by its SET instructions, slot 1, frames 0 to 7) made by 0x49BA00 at the sprite clock and stepped by the sprite scheduler on the even substeps (0x475360, 0x54F5D7): a new role or variant byte starts a figure that shows nothing before the first due pass (62 ms, strictly later, 0x4758F0), an applicant the pool does not return keeps the figure that stands, and the window's close ends it (0x49B7B4); the screen-space draw takes no camera turn (flag 0x40000); the employed-tab figure deliberately shares the hire-box layout as EXT:staff-employee-view, not native applicant sourcing", "the control depth word (+0xE0, the z register 0x476A70) and exact viewport/raster parity with the original's sprite pass"),
		("UI-086", "paths, queues and unowned land retain the native class 10..12 records; default live placed-object fills now read the exact current economy binding's Repair (PC object +0x44, SaveAttraction.StateOfRepair), round to stored float, truncate, mask the low byte and use the native integer 16.16 ramp (248,0,0 at 0; 248,200,0 at 50; 48,252,0 at 100; alpha 255, 0x5f09a0). Absent, read-only, mismatched or malformed state retains the old magenta fallback. Native cell-class/track priority, neighbour outlines, footprints and item dots remain incomplete; independent host excitement, thought and happiness overlays keep their existing precedence rather than native value-mode dispatch", "native value modes 2/3 (excitement 0x4e0860 and satisfaction 0x4e1e30), their controls and land modes (2444..2447, 2455..2457), the object cell classes 1..9 beyond the repair-ramp fill (read: 0x5f2050 gives a cell without an object the class 10, 11 or 12, a track-record cell (0x536450) 9 and an object cell the class of its owner thing, 0x4dd4e0 +0x4ac 0 -> 1 (8 on an extension or type-0x15 cell that is not type 4), 1 -> 2, 2 -> 3, 3 -> 4..7 by the type word +0x32, each shown by a bit of the map object's +0x18 or its +0x1c mode in 0x5f2380; not ported: their per-class visibility and the track-record class 9), the cell-priority order of 0x5f2fd0, open-status neighbour outlines/style 8 (0x5f2a94), item dots and footprints (0x5f44d0), and real-data/native rendered comparison; default repair semantics alone do not establish pixel equivalence"),
		("UI-091", "staff radios use independently persisted and validated role chains (+0x210), with explicit whole-role fallback for malformed original chains and read-only compatibility projection for older own saves; visitor radios project live guests onto the ThingPool used chain, with an explicit ascending-ID fallback only for pool-free fixtures; visitor position failure still clears the selection, while staff identity survives unavailable coordinates; the panels slide out of the HUD arm and back in as the drawer 0x4a14f0 does, started by 0x4a2590 (ten 20 ms ticks, geometry of ArmDrawer, the visitors' panel waiting in the arm's slot 2 until the staff panel is away, retract button shown with the slide out), and the camera follow has no smoothing of its own (the per-frame matrix blend of 0x42b1c0 runs only for the mode bits 0x3c of 0x790ab0, of which the camera setter 0x42ab20 sets only the ride bit 4: it belongs to the ride view, UI-094)", "retained visitor position-loss behavior; what the close message 0x1001d8 does when the arm retracts a locator panel inside 0x4b3f60 (the panel procedure zeroes the mode word 0x7cc2f0 after 0x4b3f60 set it, so opening a locator while one is out may leave its radios dead; not ported, a locator opened while one of its kind is out keeps the panel out without retracting it); exact-head C# validation and real-data visual comparison"),
		("UI-092", "the per-employee window uses ThingPool order, captured-target title rename and position-independent locator identity; its portrait is the original's independent clone of the member's sprite source (the source is the original's: StaffSpriteState, made by the constructors, the drop and the rest's end, deleted by the pick-up and the rest, stepped by the sprite scheduler on the even substeps, 0x475360): the window's refresh makes the full copy (0x486530 -> 0x475CF0, flags (f & ~0x200) | 0x50000, scale 8.0), every update (message 0x1E) the partial copy (0x486610 -> 0x475E10) while the member has a source, the clone keeps its own due time and interval and plays on by its own clock when the source is gone, a member without a source at the refresh gets no clone and none later, the close deletes it (0x486630); employee-only nominal 2.4 geometry at integer feet (526,476) from its inherited inner rectangle", "the staff's sprite placement (0x475480: the source's x, y, z and heading words are not kept, so the clone's heading is the member's current sector), the window depth word (+0xE0) and the z register, the saved sprite records of an original save (SAVE-013: a member without a source gets a fresh stand source) and exact viewport/raster parity"),
		("UI-094", "the ride view retains the camera-car/prototype eye and shared OriginalProjection; the seat's rotation is blended with the previous frame's as 0x42ca0d does (a = (1000 - dt) x 0.0005 with the original's frame time: whole milliseconds plus one, 100 above 200) and the free look is applied after it, the view axes being the camera matrix rows (0x56b940: direction the third, up the second), where OpenTPW's blended basis is made orthonormal again and its first ride frame starts unblended (the original blends it with the matrix of the last ride, or with the identity of the camera init 0x42a9ee); static now resets to 300 ms on an observed Boolean ride/terrain-eye edge, with positivity latched before elapsed-time subtraction (0x54faf7, 0x54fb20), the mask 0x16 naming only the walk and ride bits (no writer sets bit 0x10); the crowd sentence counts around the hover cell 0x7b05cc, the cursor ray's cell clamped to the edge cell for an off-grid hit, which the overview refreshes and the ride keeps (Level.HoverCell, 0x45d560, 0x54f875); host adaptations remain for single-sample monotonic timing, frame eligibility/initialization, the free-walk mapping, and the unchanged procedural noise", "native frame-gate/session lifecycle; native noise sequence coupling and invisible window; the coaster and prototype fallback frames of a ride without a seat; exact-head C# and real-data visual validation"),
		("UI-095", "leaving the ride view restores its prior camera instance, including the host terrain walk, and re-centres the host park camera on the exit cell of the ride whose entrance lies under its target (0x42a340: the owner thing of type 3 with CannotRide 0; its mExitPos is read at 0x42a22e) with the original's look direction (0x42a1d0: the link byte (+0xd) of that cell, a 0x44-byte record at *0x7cf6ec + 0x294, masked with 0x55: 1 gives pi, 4 pi/2, 0x10 0, 0x40 3pi/2) and, like 0x42a1d0, only the target and the yaw; the byte of an exit cell is written by the placement commit (shape type 10 through the switch 0x529164: 0x5292b2 by 0x5227e0, an entrance's own by 0x5293c3) and by the track editor and the cell reset (0x5227f0 from 0x53b280, 0x536490), which ParkCellMap.WriteFootprint and the track code carry (QueueLinkAt), so the yaw rule fires for placed rides; the original's park camera is its own pose (yaw, height and the 0x42b1c0 motion) that OpenTPW's host camera does not reproduce", "divergent saved mExitPos values and the native order of overlapping things in a cell's list; the park camera's own pose"),
		("UI-100", "the path and queue tools choose the link pointer (code 8, flag 0x816d60: 0x535c72, 0x535d02), the end pointer (code 0xb, flag 0x816d4c: 0x535ae5, 0x535b3d: the last cell of the line is an existing path cell, or the ride's own queue cell) and the no-place pointer of a refused line (0x527950, set at 0x533933) from the line preview, the cash pointer by the line's money stop; the kart and water track lines take the end pointer from the track chooser's word 0x816d4c (set with its answer 0xb at 0x53a1c6 when the line meets a tile of its own kind) and the cash pointer from its word 0x816d5c (set at 0x539fb6 by the money test 0x539f95 that refuses a tile the line cannot pay for), both read from the tile ghost; not drawn: the crosshair's art (CCro.tga is not in the game data), so OpenTPW keeps the system pointer there", "the crosshair art (CCro.tga) in the game data"),
